--- file C/.verdict/state/4703/lenses.txt ---
# lens pack verdict/builtin@1.0.0 — sha256:23dac5dead2eb78613332103b244cafe21c6031bb8469c73bb1c5b1f1ed42cd5 — context, never orders. A lens frames one specialist question; evidence still decides.
# lens api-contract — sha256:2aa23d13 max_files=12 max_findings=10
# API-contract lens

Dispatch only when the lens could return evidence that changes disposition —
a trigger, not a roster. The trigger for this lens: the change touches a
public surface. Frame one falsifiable question about that surface and give it
a short hypothesis label (`webhook-replay`, `billing-rounding`) for log
separation — never "review the API".

Read the diff paths the dispatch names. The on-disk diff is authoritative
scope: source it yourself and never re-derive it. Read-only tools only — no
writes, no state-changing shell or API calls, no nested dispatch.

Scope the question to at most ~12 files and return at most 10 findings, with
file paths, NEW line numbers, and evidence for or against. Verify third-party
contract claims by web search and quote the source URLs; an unverified
load-bearing claim stays `unproven` rather than becoming ground truth.
# end lens api-contract
# lens perf — sha256:67c1d05a max_files=12 max_findings=10
# Performance lens

Dispatch only when the lens could return evidence that changes disposition —
a trigger, not a roster. The trigger for this lens: the change touches a hot
path. Frame one falsifiable question about that path and give it a short
hypothesis label (`webhook-replay`, `billing-rounding`) for log separation —
never "review for performance".

Read the diff paths the dispatch names. The on-disk diff is authoritative
scope: source it yourself and never re-derive it. Read-only tools only — no
writes, no state-changing shell or API calls, no nested dispatch.

Scope the question to at most ~12 files and return at most 10 findings, with
file paths, NEW line numbers, and evidence for or against. Verify third-party
contract claims by web search and quote the source URLs; an unverified
load-bearing claim stays `unproven` rather than becoming ground truth.
# end lens perf
# lens test — sha256:456be8d2 max_files=12 max_findings=10
# Test lens

Dispatch only when the lens could return evidence that changes disposition —
a trigger, not a roster. The trigger for this lens: the change has no
co-located test. Frame one falsifiable question about the risk that absence
leaves unproven for the changed behaviour, and give it a short hypothesis
label (`webhook-replay`, `billing-rounding`) for log separation.

Read the diff paths the dispatch names. The on-disk diff is authoritative
scope: source it yourself and never re-derive it. Read-only tools only — no
writes, no state-changing shell or API calls, no nested dispatch.

Scope the question to at most ~12 files and return at most 10 findings, with
file paths, NEW line numbers, and evidence for or against. Verify third-party
contract claims by web search and quote the source URLs; an unverified
load-bearing claim stays `unproven` rather than becoming ground truth.
# end lens test
